caption: Generating an importer
tags: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage
title: $:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/generator
type: text/vnd.tiddlywiki

Once a profile works against your data, you can bake it into an
//importer//: a small plugin that somebody else installs and uses
without ever seeing the profile, the Console or the editor.  They get a
sidebar tab named for their data, a box to paste into, ''Convert'' and
''Apply''.

!!! Making one

# In the Console, select the profile and click ''Generate importer…'' (the same button sits on the profile tiddler itself).  The generator opens with sensible defaults filled in.
# Check the ''publisher'' and ''slug''.  Together they make the plugin's title, `$:/plugins/<publisher>/<slug>`, and the slug also names the importer's working data, so two importers in one wiki must differ.
# Give it a ''name'', a ''tab caption'' the recipient will click, and an ''introduction'' that says where the JSON comes from and what comes out.  Label the ''Convert'' button for the data: //Stage invoices// beats //Convert//.
# Pick ''sample data'' if you have some.  It ships in the pack behind a ''Try it with the sample'' button, and its shape is recorded so the panel can tell the recipient when their JSON does not look like what the profile expects.
# Click ''Generate''.

The pack is installed in this wiki at once, so the new tab appears in
your own sidebar exactly as the recipient will see it.  Hand it over by
dragging the plugin tiddler onto their wiki, or download it:

* ''Download pack'' — for a wiki that already has the JSON Convert runtime.
* ''Download pack + runtime'' — one file for a wiki with nothing installed.  A wiki that already has the same or a newer runtime keeps its own and takes just the pack.

!!! What goes in the pack

* A copy of the profile, with `"format": 1` stamped in, under the pack's own title so an ordinary tiddler can never shadow it by accident.
* Every custom transform the profile references, copied with its name.  A transform that does not exist is a generation error, not a surprise for the recipient.  Transforms that ship with the runtime are not copied.
* The sample and its shape fingerprint, if you chose one.
* The panel tiddler: the tab caption, the labels, the collision default, the lowest runtime version the pack needs, and this studio's URL, so every "ask whoever made this" message in the panel points back here.

See [[Importer pack fields|$:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/usage/reference/pack-fields]] for the exact fields.

!!! Regenerating

The [[Studio|$:/plugins/crosseye/json-convert-studio/Studio]] page lists
every importer made here, says when its profile has been edited since,
and has a ''Regenerate…'' button that opens the generator with all of
that importer's settings and the version bumped.  A recipient who drags
in the new file gets the newer pack and TiddlyWiki discards the old one.
If you have lost the original profile, dragging a pack into this wiki
puts its profile in the Console's dropdown, where you can edit it and
generate afresh; ''Regenerate…'' then uses the copy inside the pack.

!!! JavaScript

A pack carries JavaScript only when it includes a JavaScript transform.
The generator says so when it does.  The recipient should take such a
pack only from someone they trust — which, for a hand-delivered
importer, they already do.
